Wrap a masked texture as the RDP does

A tile's mask makes the RDP wrap that axis every 2^mask texels. It does so whatever the tile's size: a tile bigger
than its mask repeats the masked part across the tile. Fast3D trims a texture to its mask only when the mask is at
least as big as the tile, and otherwise takes the mask for stale tile state and wraps at the texture's whole size.

WCW/nWo Revenge draws the Option menu's steel plate from a 64x64 texture with a 64x64 tile and a mask of 32 texels on
both axes, so the N64 repeats the texture's top-left 32x32 corner. Fast3D repeated the whole 64x64 texture, whose
other three corners have their light and dark patches in other places, so the plate's shading did not match the
original's as it scrolled. Fast3D now always honours the mask, in the four texture imports and in the draw that
works out the texture's wrap period.

Patch 0009 keeps the masks in the texture cache's key, so a texture drawn with and without a mask has an entry for
each.

